From 234bf0b8ca7c64637739d4f05aa0e859761a16a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Malard <malard@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:09:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [Peripherals] Power off controllers on quit

CPeripherals powers off controllers when it receives OnQuit, which the
application announces under the System flag. It has never received it:
from 8cc58c4578 it tested for flag == Player, and since 464529b269
dropped that test it registers for Player announcements only. It now
registers for System, the only flag its handler acts on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit f685ec35f889c16f7cb98ad8e9cac8fbbc24127f)
---
 xbmc/peripherals/Peripherals.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/peripherals/Peripherals.cpp b/xbmc/peripherals/Peripherals.cpp
index c94f8bc..5cc8f40 100644
--- a/xbmc/peripherals/Peripherals.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/peripherals/Peripherals.cpp
@@ -141,7 +141,7 @@ void CPeripherals::Initialise()
   m_eventScanner->Start();
 
   CServiceBroker::GetAppMessenger()->RegisterReceiver(this);
-  CServiceBroker::GetAnnouncementManager()->AddAnnouncer(this, ANNOUNCEMENT::Player);
+  CServiceBroker::GetAnnouncementManager()->AddAnnouncer(this, ANNOUNCEMENT::System);
 
   // Register for GUI messages
   CGUIComponent* gui = CServiceBroker::GetGUI();
